3:Each use case has its purpose, what fails it, and its minimum acceptance. U1–U3 are the owner's request; U4–U6 are
4-*proposed* until the owner accepts them. A use case wins over a requirement that conflicts with it.
5-
6-## U1 — See what memory a project has
7-- **Purpose:** the owner learns which memory exists: `AGENTS.md`, `project-memory/` (`INDEX.md`, `entries/`, `work/`,
8-  `journal/`), its caches under `project-memory/.cache/`, and the agent memory the guidelines place outside the repo.
9-- **Fails if:** a memory location the guidelines name exists and the report does not list it, or the report lists one
10-  that does not exist.
11-- **Minimum acceptance:** run on this repo and on a fixture project with every location present, the report lists each
12-  location and says present or absent, matching the files.
13-
14-## U2 — Know what breaks the guidelines
15-- **Purpose:** each requirement a tool can check is checked, with its id, its level and the evidence.
16-- **Fails if:** a requirement whose check is `tool` or `git` is not checked, a result has no evidence (a file and line,
17-  or a command and its output), or a MUST that fails is shown as passing.
18-- **Minimum acceptance:** a fixture project with one planted break per checkable requirement gets exactly the
19-  requirements whose fails_if that break meets reported as failing (two ids that share one fails_if, such as K6.1a
20-  and K6.2, fail together), with the planted file named.
21-
22:## U3 — Be warned at the start of a session
23-- **Purpose:** an agent starting work is told, in a few lines, what is missing or failing, without reading the report.
24-- **Fails if:** a MUST that fails or could not run, or a missing `AGENTS.md`, is not in the warning, or the warning
25-  holds anything else.
26-- **Minimum acceptance:** the session-start hook prints one line per MUST that fails or could not run and for a
27-  missing `AGENTS.md`, and nothing when there are none.
28-
29-## U4 — Name what needs a reviewer (*proposed*)
30-- **Purpose:** the requirements a tool cannot judge are listed for a person, so the report does not look complete when
31-  it is not.
32-- **Fails if:** a requirement whose check is `reviewer` is reported as passing or failing by the tool.
33-- **Minimum acceptance:** the report has a section listing every reviewer-only requirement by id.
34-
35-## U5 — Never change memory (*proposed*)
36-- **Purpose:** running the tool is always safe.
37-- **Fails if:** after a run, `git status --short` shows any change other than the report file.
38-- **Minimum acceptance:** a test runs the tool on a fixture and compares `git status` before and after.
39-
40-## U6 — Work on any project (*proposed*)
41-- **Purpose:** the tool checks the project it is pointed at, not only this repo.
42-- **Fails if:** a project path given on the command line is ignored, or a missing path is reported as an empty memory.
